Z||000005||Bazooka||09-13-2001||11:06 PM||||V8FieroGT,<BR>   What type of engine do you have? If its a SBC with a stock TPI and Throttle Body you could be gasping for air at about 4500 rpm like I was. My solution was a Lingenfelter Lower Base, High Flow Runners and Edelbrock High Flow Throttle Body which all allow plenty of air to be ssucked down at the higher rpm's.<BR> <A HREF="http://hometown.aol.com/m34chev/myhomepage/auto.html" TARGET=_blank>http://hometown.aol.com/m34chev/myhomepage/auto.html</A>  <BR>************************************<BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by v8fieroGT:<BR><B>I just put a cold air intake on my gt yesterday and It gave me some bottom end but totaly killed my top end. I can get to 80 no problem but as soon as i start passing 80 it is a lot slower. Did anyone else experience this or does anyone know why it's doing this.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||1
